WEBVTT

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:07.250
Too bad!

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:09.880
This way's a dead end.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:13.670
Let's do this, Ibara!

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:14.790
Hell yeah!

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:23.210
What?!

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:29.380
Heads up, Ryo!

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:30.250
Get 'em, four-eyes!

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.250
Nice slicing and dicing.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:40.040
Man, Ryo is so cool!

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.790
"I just don't care anymore"

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:09.580
A reply thrown out

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:14.380
Briefly blooming then briefly falling, over and over

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.920
Left feeling unsatisfied

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:20.830
Yes, day by day, I walked on

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:23.130
Cry, futurity, gloomy

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:27.130
The twilight still out of reach

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.500
Don't lose your way

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:32.670
Tighten the twine of dreams

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.080
Take me so high

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:37.920
Start running to a brand new life

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:40.420
Everything I have in my hand

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:44.130
Holding onto seven colors

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:46.000
Go ahead, make my day

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.380
I'll use this fist to rebel even harder!

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:51.830
Everything I have in my hand

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:55.580
Sketching ideals and hopes

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:57.170
I won't let you down

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:00.460
I'll let this flower bloom forever!

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:04.130
Believe myself

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:16.000
<b>Black Team</b>

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.290
Whoa! That blew me away!

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:19.960
You two were in total synch!

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:21.830
Wow! You think so?!

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:23.080
We make a good team, huh?

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:24.250
Don't be ridiculous.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.330
He's just shy.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:29.000
Tell me, where'd you learn those sick moves?

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:32.170
Well, to be honest... uh...

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:35.750
<b>Go home</b>

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:35.750
<b>And be a family man</b>

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:35.630
Uppercut into an overhead. That's the key to victory!

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:38.880
Fighting games taught me!

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:39.670
Huh?

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.210
Child's play.

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:42.540
So, uh...

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:44.880
I wonder what caused that man to become a vessel?

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:46.250
Oh my gosh, babe!

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:48.170
I'm so sorry about earlier.

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:50.500
The whole thing was a misunderstanding.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:52.540
What? Seriously?

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:54.330
Forgive me! I'm really sorry!

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:55.750
It's cool, no problem.

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:57.210
C'mon, let's go.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:57.960
Okay.

00:02:58.250 --> 00:02:59.540
It is a problem.
It's totally a problem!<b></b>

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:00.670
Just relax.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:01.670
Well...

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:04.750
We know it did cause him some internal strife.

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:09.170
The fact that Oni are taking
advantage of such trivial fears,

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:13.330
means the gap between our realm and
the nether realm is growing especially thin.

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:16.250
So what you're saying is, the world is in danger!

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:18.460
But that's okay, because justice will prevail!

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:22.000
How many times do I have to tell you? We're not heroes!

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:24.130
Th-then let's become heroes!

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:25.540
We can do it!

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:26.330
Excuse me.

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:31.750
Um, I wanted to ask, what happens
if we can't save a vessel?

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:33.500
Nothing good.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.380
C-can you be a little more specific?

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:37.460
We exist to prevent that very scenario.

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:41.130
You're right! With our powers combined,
we can save everybody!

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:44.880
Ugh, you're driving me crazy!
Get it through your head, man!

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:46.460
Kaede! Take it easy!

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:47.580
We've got trouble!

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:50.330
My sister is coming!

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.080
Table check.

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:54.880
Vase check.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:56.420
Ibara check.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:58.960
Don't lump me in with the vase!

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:02.790
Everything's spotless!

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:05.170
I'm done cleaning the bathroom!

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:07.540
I put in new rolls of toilet paper, too!

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.920
I've put out tea and snacks.

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:12.210
We're fully prepared for her arrival.

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:14.170
Thank you all!

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:15.920
I'm so glad we made it in time!

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:19.130
Yeah! Everything goes quicker with teamwork!

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:21.460
You can put those away any time now.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:25.330
I'm curious.

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:28.500
What is your older sister like, Oka?

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:30.460
I'm not sure where to start...

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:33.790
I hear that she's super intimidating,
though I've never met her myself.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:37.040
But we're talking about your sister, right?

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:41.290
Yes. It's true that we're sisters, but that's not all...

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:43.750
To put it simply, she's also our boss.

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:45.080
Our boss?

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:48.380
Nobody told me that we had any bosses around here.

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:51.130
So how high up on the totem pole is she?

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:53.420
Are we talking like store manager or area manager?

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:55.250
What are we, a retail chain?

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:56.750
Even higher than that.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:01.000
She oversees her very own crew.

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:04.750
Th-the Godsister...

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:07.880
We refer to them as the Black Team.

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:10.250
But officially, they're...

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.250
SHIRUKO BISCUITS!

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:14.790
Did you say Shiruko biscuits?

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:16.670
Is that supposed to be their name?

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.580
No, that's not it.

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:20.290
I'm confused.

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:21.080
Not good!

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:22.880
Did you eat a bad biscuit?

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:26.080
The Shiruko biscuits...

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:28.630
are missing!

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:32.790
We have plenty of other snacks, though.

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:35.920
The only snacks that matters
right now are Shiruko biscuits.

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:38.830
Without them, we're doomed.

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:41.460
Huh? Huh?!

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:45.710
So, these Shiruko things are some kinda food?

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:50.170
Let's see here.

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:53.960
Shiruko biscuits, Shiruko biscuits...

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:55.670
Oh! There we go!

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.130
Whew, what a relief. There's one bag left!

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:04.920
Uh, hi there...

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:09.750
I'm really sorry!

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:13.210
But I gotta get those Shiruko biscuits, no matter what!

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:15.420
Pwetty pwease?

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:19.210
I have to bring some back or
my boss is gonna fly off the handle!

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:25.790
Uh, is something the matter?

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:27.920
Just my imagination.

00:06:29.670 --> 00:06:31.750
Sorry that my boss gave you a hard time.

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:33.380
N-not a problem.

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:36.460
Those Shiruko biscuits are pretty tasty, huh?

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:44.920
Good stuff!

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:47.500
Wait, is that Kakeru?

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:47.830
<b>Muscles</b>

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:47.830
<b>4 Life</b>

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:50.710
Yo! Kakeru!

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:54.040
That hurt...

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:56.080
Sorry, I wasn't looking. Are you okay?

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:02.380
I am so dead.

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:03.670
Everything okay?

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:06.420
I hope that you're not hurt.

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:07.880
Uh, I'm okay.

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:11.290
Oh crap! I got juice on you!

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:13.000
I am so sorry!

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:15.670
Let me wipe it off. Um... I think I have some tissues.

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:15.460
Doesn't matter.

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:20.540
What a badass!

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:27.540
Oka!

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:30.210
I've missed you so much! How long's it been?

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:32.250
One week? One month? One year?

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:36.290
Well... more like 3 days.

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:39.500
How've you been? Everything okay?

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:40.290
Hm? Hm?

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:42.290
D-doing just fine, thanks.

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:44.670
Really? That's wonderful!

00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:45.880
Boys!

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:49.380
We come bearing gifts!

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:53.080
Look, Oka! We brought all of your favorite things!

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:55.330
If you need more, I'll send them to fetch it right away!

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:57.210
Th-thanks so much, big sis...

00:07:57.880 --> 00:07:59.000
"Big sis"?!

00:07:59.460 --> 00:08:01.630
Yes. This is my older sister.

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:03.540
I recognize you.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:06.540
Thanks for earlier.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.130
You've met before?

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:09.000
Just briefly.

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:12.170
He's our newest member, Kakeru.

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:13.540
My name's Kakeru Miwa.

00:08:13.750 --> 00:08:15.170
Benio Myojin.

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:17.170
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:22.250
The pleasure is all mine, Biscuit Fetcher.

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:25.540
Let me introduce my crew.

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:27.580
This is Issa Inuzuka.

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:29.790
And over there is Ukon Kijima.

00:08:29.790 --> 00:08:31.500
Give me your digits later, ladies.

00:08:32.920 --> 00:08:33.960
I'll take those.

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:34.920
Appreciate it.

00:08:35.960 --> 00:08:37.330
He smells like melons...

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:41.420
Let's get down to business.

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:42.500
Okay.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:45.130
We're in need of some extra man power.

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:47.500
I was hoping the Midnight Sun could help out.

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:48.830
"Midnight Sun"?

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:51.290
That refers to us, the White Team.

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:53.290
I assume you're hunting a Shinja.

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:54.540
That's right.

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:58.330
Seems like they've grown smarter lately.
It's become tough to track them down.

00:08:58.540 --> 00:09:01.080
They're terrified of us, so they try to hide.

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:03.880
Wait, are you expecting us to defeat them?

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:07.750
Only we members of Volcanic Glass
are capable of bringing down a Shinja.

00:09:08.670 --> 00:09:11.750
We want to lure them out of hiding by using you as bait.

00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:15.250
All right.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:18.670
Listen up. Do not engage the Oni when you find it.

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:21.080
The first thing you should do is contact us.

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:27.920
Shikizakura.

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:33.380
Shikizakura.

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:36.000
So, Oka's sister.

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:38.290
She's pretty overbearing, huh?

00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:41.540
I get the impression she thinks of us
more like pawns than anything.

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:44.290
Seriously, who asks for help with that kind of attitude?

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:46.290
I... I'm so sorry.

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:49.250
Well, it's true we can't handle this alone.

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:50.420
That's right.

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:55.330
The Black Team deals with far worse carnage
than we do on a regular basis.

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:59.500
Um, what's that "Shinja" thing you mentioned yesterday?

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:02.500
Is it different from regular Oni somehow?

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:08.290
Shinja are Oni that have fully consumed their vessel.

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:12.380
Do you mean that...?

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:15.630
Yeah, what happens to the person they possessed?

00:10:16.290 --> 00:10:21.790
Vessels that completely lose sight of themselves and
get eaten by Oni can never return to being human.

00:10:22.540 --> 00:10:24.880
All they do is find more people to devour,
one after the other.

00:10:26.460 --> 00:10:28.790
So, the fact a Shinja showed up means...

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:32.170
...there's a vessel who couldn't be saved.

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:34.040
How awful...

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:35.830
I'm sorry.

00:10:37.250 --> 00:10:38.420
I'm such a failure.

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:41.040
It's not your fault, Lady Oka.

00:10:41.630 --> 00:10:43.250
No one deserves the blame.

00:10:44.130 --> 00:10:45.830
I'll do the best I can.

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:48.250
Let's all do our best!

00:10:48.880 --> 00:10:51.170
That way we can prevent this from happening ever again!

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:52.170
That's impossible.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:57.330
There is a limit to how many people
that we can save by ourselves.

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:03.630
Because the reality is, we can't be like
those ideal heroes you see in fiction.

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:09.630
We're here.

00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:12.630
<b>NINJA</b>

00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:12.630
<b>KINGDOM</b>

00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:12.630
<b>ISE</b>

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:11.250
Ise's Ninja Kingdom.

00:11:12.920 --> 00:11:15.330
Our intel says that the Shinja is here somewhere.

00:11:17.380 --> 00:11:19.040
A Shinja... hiding here...

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:22.250
It's a serious threat. Stay alert at all times.

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:23.960
Move out.

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:29.000
Okay! All done!

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:33.460
You're so lucky, I can't believe Nyanmage
asked you for a picture!

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:36.000
So "Nyanmage" is what that thing's called?

00:11:37.580 --> 00:11:38.960
You don't know about Nyanmage?!

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:40.710
But aren't you from Mie Prefecture?

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:42.500
And aren't you a ninja?

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:45.290
Enough. You guys aren't funny.

00:11:45.830 --> 00:11:47.670
I'm starting to lose confidence.

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:50.380
We came here to complete a mission, right?

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:53.710
I wish we could have come on a date instead!

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:55.290
That scared me...

00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:58.500
Well, we have two teams here.
Let's split up and get to work!

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:03.330
If you find the Shinja, report to us immediately.

00:12:03.790 --> 00:12:05.790
Don't even think of trying to lay a finger on it.

00:12:09.210 --> 00:12:12.460
<b>Commoner's</b>

00:12:09.210 --> 00:12:12.460
<b>Village</b>

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:17.130
The Shinja is definitely hiding
somewhere on the premises.

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:19.130
Huh? Among all these people?!

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:20.210
Exactly.

00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:25.040
After consuming a vessel,
Shinja always blend in with crowds of people

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:27.130
so they can hunt more prey.

00:12:28.630 --> 00:12:30.670
We have to find it before there are more victims.

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:31.880
Yes.

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:35.710
It will avoid us if we move around as a group.

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:37.580
So we'll search independently.

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:38.670
Roger.

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:45.290
Man... this is like looking for a needle in a haystack.

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:47.250
Hey, twerp.

00:12:47.880 --> 00:12:49.540
That you, Ibara? What's up?

00:12:50.630 --> 00:12:51.960
This place is bad news.

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:52.630
Huh?

00:12:52.630 --> 00:12:53.920
Is there something here?

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:55.250
The Shinja?

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:56.580
I dunno.

00:12:57.130 --> 00:13:00.000
But something powerful is definitely lurking nearby.

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:01.330
Where is it?

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:04.210
Somebody...

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:08.000
Somebody... please help...

00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:11.580
Th-there's something back there.

00:13:11.580 --> 00:13:13.040
Keep your distance!

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:14.630
But a voice was calling for help!

00:13:15.210 --> 00:13:19.250
Please... I need help...

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:21.710
Stay back, dipshit!

00:13:28.710 --> 00:13:30.250
I'm begging you, please...

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:32.710
What happened?!

00:13:33.170 --> 00:13:35.920
It's my son! He's been kidnapped!

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:37.250
A monster took him!

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:39.670
A monster?! Then it probably was...

00:13:45.580 --> 00:13:46.710
Move it, twerp!

00:13:47.830 --> 00:13:48.830
Twerp!

00:13:50.170 --> 00:13:51.250
Here it comes.

00:13:52.250 --> 00:13:53.040
Transform!

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:20.880
I can't believe it's trying to fool people with
that lame routine. How friggin' stupid.

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:24.790
This is Kakeru. I've found the Shinja!

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:26.250
I'm on my way!

00:14:26.250 --> 00:14:28.580
Remember, keep your distance and don't engage!

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:30.830
That's easier said than done...

00:14:35.790 --> 00:14:36.580
Dodge it!

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:41.500
What the heck was that?!

00:14:42.210 --> 00:14:43.710
Now this is gonna be fun.

00:14:49.880 --> 00:14:51.170
Hey! Quit running!

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:53.540
I have to!

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:55.580
They said don't engage!

00:14:57.710 --> 00:14:59.250
Turn around and fight, dammit!

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:03.250
No way!

00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:05.500
Come on! Go punch it!

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:07.330
Nuh-uh!

00:15:08.710 --> 00:15:09.670
Just go!

00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:11.960
Screw it!

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:21.460
Hey. You an Oni?

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:22.960
Huh?

00:15:23.170 --> 00:15:24.540
It recognizes Ibara?!

00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:28.750
I see now! You're a loser that failed to become a Shinja!

00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:33.210
Don't lump me in with the rest
of you nasty, man-eating bastards.

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:36.210
I ain't like you. I'm the almighty Ibara!

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:37.880
How pathetic!

00:15:37.880 --> 00:15:39.630
You haven't consumed a human!

00:15:42.380 --> 00:15:43.670
What a waste of time.

00:15:44.710 --> 00:15:47.170
Answer me! Why are you doing this?!

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:52.250
You want to know why? It's simple,
all we're doing is granting the desires of man!

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:53.460
The desires of man?!

00:15:53.790 --> 00:15:58.080
Indeed. Surrendering your body
and mind entirely to someone else...

00:15:58.080 --> 00:16:01.210
That is the ultimate desire of all humanity!

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:03.500
You're full of crap!

00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:08.250
If you're truly an Oni, then you must have heard
the voices of human souls like I have!

00:16:08.670 --> 00:16:14.290
They all want the same thing, to have
their very own heart fade away into nothing!

00:16:14.460 --> 00:16:15.380
Shut your face!

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:24.670
Okay, twerp. Now's our chance.

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:26.790
Finish it off.

00:16:30.080 --> 00:16:31.210
I can't.

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:33.210
Because he's still...

00:16:33.670 --> 00:16:34.500
human.

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:36.170
We have to save him!

00:16:37.500 --> 00:16:38.880
Dumbass! Don't fall for it!

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:47.880
What are you doing?!

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:50.250
That isn't human, it's an Oni!

00:16:50.630 --> 00:16:53.460
If we don't take it out, then it'll just devour more people!

00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:55.460
But...

00:16:58.420 --> 00:16:59.540
Here comes the calvary!

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:08.580
We have to vanquish the Shinja.

00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:12.420
That's the only funeral we can offer
for the souls of the departed.

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:15.920
Brace yourself.

00:17:17.830 --> 00:17:20.290
Sorry I'm late! I'll back you up!

00:17:24.330 --> 00:17:25.330
Haruko!

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:28.670
It's just gonna run?!

00:17:28.670 --> 00:17:29.330
Follow it!

00:17:29.540 --> 00:17:30.250
Right!

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:31.830
Ouch...

00:17:32.790 --> 00:17:33.540
You okay?

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:34.250
Yeah.

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:36.080
Chase after the Shinja, Kaede!

00:17:36.080 --> 00:17:36.920
On it.

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:48.170
It's all over the damn place.

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:50.580
It's gonna get away!

00:18:11.330 --> 00:18:12.420
Wh-what just happened?

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:15.920
It's still alive. Just hang back, kitten.

00:18:16.210 --> 00:18:16.790
Huh?

00:18:40.130 --> 00:18:42.170
He's back... to being human...

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:44.670
No. We just haven't finished it.

00:18:46.540 --> 00:18:49.250
Stand aside. We'll handle the rest ourselves.

00:18:50.460 --> 00:18:51.630
What does that mean?

00:18:52.170 --> 00:18:53.540
You can't just kill him.

00:18:54.880 --> 00:18:55.830
I'm sorry...

00:18:58.250 --> 00:19:03.130
Daddy's been so busy lately,
I haven't had any time to play with you...

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:13.960
That's okay. But please come home some day.

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:18.040
Then we can... play again...

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:20.920
Okay... it's a promi...

00:19:31.920 --> 00:19:33.250
Don't buy into it.

00:19:33.630 --> 00:19:36.080
It's nothing more than a desperate whine.

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:41.920
Why?!

00:19:42.420 --> 00:19:44.290
Why did you kill him?!

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:46.250
That was basically murder!

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:47.040
Wrong.

00:19:48.710 --> 00:19:50.880
That man ate his own son.

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:52.130
Huh?

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:54.710
What does that mean...?

00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:55.920
Exactly what I said.

00:19:56.580 --> 00:19:58.500
Oni are always Oni no matter where you go.

00:19:59.130 --> 00:19:59.830
But then-

00:20:10.210 --> 00:20:11.330
Take him away.

00:20:11.330 --> 00:20:12.210
Ma'am.

00:20:19.670 --> 00:20:20.290
Kakeru!

00:20:20.290 --> 00:20:21.000
Miwa!

00:20:27.750 --> 00:20:28.830
Big sis...

00:20:29.880 --> 00:20:32.000
Was Ibara your real target this whole time?

00:20:33.380 --> 00:20:35.000
Maybe. Who can say?

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:39.040
Let's move.

00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:51.830
I hope that this moment never ends

00:20:52.130 --> 00:20:55.830
I hope that it continues for decades to come

00:20:57.330 --> 00:21:02.250
Becoming unable to even wear pretty outfits

00:21:02.630 --> 00:21:06.540
In a world where only I have passed on

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:10.710
The cider I disliked that day

00:21:10.710 --> 00:21:13.040
The cry of the missing cicadas

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:15.330
Drowning into fate

00:21:15.330 --> 00:21:18.500
Not knowing how to struggle

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:23.290
It's almost as if I'm invisible to everyone

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:27.210
I don't even feel the urge to resist

00:21:28.460 --> 00:21:32.960
After you helped pulled me along

00:21:33.420 --> 00:21:36.790
I saw the beautiful colors of the world

00:21:36.790 --> 00:21:39.380
In the season of blooming cherry blossoms

00:21:39.380 --> 00:21:43.540
Captivated by that innocent smile

00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:47.500
There is nothing that can't be changed

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:51.630
And that's true of any sad future too, right?

00:22:24.540 --> 00:22:26.790
We've succeeded in capturing Ibara.

00:22:27.920 --> 00:22:29.460
We're returning to base now.

00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:38.210
Oh man, what's gonna happen to me now?!

00:22:38.210 --> 00:22:38.960
Doesn't matter.

00:22:38.960 --> 00:22:42.000
Uh, okay, then who was that
important-looking old guy at the end?

00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:42.630
Doesn't matter.

00:22:42.630 --> 00:22:44.880
Then at least tell me what this sweet smell is!

00:22:44.880 --> 00:22:45.540
Melon.

00:22:45.920 --> 00:22:47.750
Next time: Partner.

00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:51.000
<b>Partner</b>

00:22:47.750 --> 00:22:49.710
He stole the best part of the preview!

00:22:49.710 --> 00:22:50.580
Doesn't matter.
